{
  "an6.51:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.51 ",
  "an6.51:0.2": "5. About Dhammika ",
  "an6.51:0.3": "With Ānanda ",
  "an6.51:1.1": "Then Venerable Ānanda went up to Venerable Sāriputta, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "an6.51:1.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, Ānanda sat down to one side, and said to Sāriputta: ",
  "an6.51:2.1": "“Reverend Sāriputta, how does a mendicant get to hear a teaching they haven’t heard before? How do they remember those teachings they have heard? How do they keep exercising the teachings with which they are already familiar? And how do they come to understand what they haven’t understood before?” ",
  "an6.51:2.2": "“Well, Venerable Ānanda, you’re very learned. ",
  "an6.51:2.3": "Why don’t you clarify this yourself?” ",
  "an6.51:2.4": "“Well then, Reverend Sāriputta, listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "an6.51:2.5": "“Yes, reverend,” Sāriputta replied. ",
  "an6.51:2.6": "Ānanda said this: ",
  "an6.51:3.1": "“Reverend Sāriputta, take a mendicant who memorizes the teaching—",
  "an6.51:3.2": "statements, mixed prose & verse, discussions, verses, inspired exclamations, legends, stories of past lives, amazing stories, and elaborations. ",
  "an6.51:3.3": "Then, just as they learned and memorized it, they teach others in detail, make them recite in detail, they rehearse it themselves in detail, and they think about and consider the teaching in their heart, examining it with the mind. ",
  "an6.5